+## Return to the tested upstream baseline
+
+Stop the branded service before starting the baseline because both use port
+`9982`:
+
+```powershell
+docker compose -f .\\docker\\ralue\\compose.yml down
+docker compose -f .\\docker\\ralue\\compose.baseline.yml up -d
+```
+
+The baseline image `ralue/editor:upstream-26.04.2.4` is kept locally and the
+source checkpoint is tagged `ralue-upstream-26.04.2.4`.
+
+## MVP acceptance evidence
+
+Validated locally on 2026-09-23:
+
+- discovery, capabilities, logo, favicon, and browser bundle returned HTTP 200;
+- product name is `Ralue Editor`, source version is `26.04.2.4`, and the
+  deployable browser revision is `a1e2604001`;
+- the engine binary `libmergedlo.so` has the same SHA-256 in the upstream and
+  branded images: `cd949dab5bdc1c7158da06debd9fff493833eed581149cb7118c00fa71103c1e`;
+- a real DOCX opened through the existing WOPI host, was edited, saved into a
+  new immutable version, closed, and reopened with the edit present;
+- the active DOCX converted through `/cool/convert-to/pdf` to a valid,
+  visually inspected one-page PDF;
+- the second build reused the exported Docker and ccache data instead of
+  restarting from zero.
+
